1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,060
[Disclaimer: This series is created
solely for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,330
All individuals, behaviors, places,
and events depicted are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:05,000
with no intention to represent or reference any
organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

4
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:06,270
Don't you think

5
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,090
we ended things a bit too abruptly?

6
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:10,940
You know why we dated back then.

7
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,180
I let you use me
to make other people jealous,

8
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,580
but I actually love you now.

9
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,090
Chris doesn't love you.

10
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:16,860
Chris loves...

11
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,130
Don't you dare say her name!

12
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,000
Stop being around Chris already.

13
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:21,280
I can't do that.

14
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,000
I love Chris.

15
00:00:23,470 --> 00:00:24,900
I know everything now.

16
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,600
Let's end things here.

17
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,800
Chris, I'm sorry...

18
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,040
Let's get back together, Chris.

19
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:45,100
I'm the only one who has never left you.

20
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,200
Chris!

21
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,900
No, don't leave me. I'm sorry...

22
00:01:05,490 --> 00:01:06,520
Go to hell!

23
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:07,720
Chris!

24
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:10,070
Chris!

25
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:11,730
Sun.

26
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:13,600
I'm here. I'm right here.

27
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,200
Chris...

28
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:19,760
I'm sorry...

29
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,910
It's okay now.

30
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:25,410
It's okay. I'm right here.

31
00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:29,020
It's going to be alright.

32
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:42,300
I'm sorry, Chris.

33
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:48,870
What are you apologizing for?

34
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:05,380
[Third Person]

35
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:16,930
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

36
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:22,610
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

37
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:26,250
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

38
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:32,670
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

39
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:42,120
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

40
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:47,570
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

41
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:51,870
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

42
00:02:51,890 --> 00:03:00,810
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

43
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:09,410
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

44
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:27,590
Stress,

45
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,050
anxiety,

46
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:30,590
or uncertainty

47
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:33,590
can make you dream about
falling from a high place.

48
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:35,960
Who was it?

49
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:38,320
Me.

50
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:40,800
Someone who has bizarre dreams

51
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:44,200
and fights the voices
in their head, like you,

52
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,410
wouldn't ask a doctor about
something so trivial.

53
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:50,990
It's my girlfriend.

54
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:54,710
The one you talk about a lot?

55
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:57,600
Yeah...

56
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,120
The one who makes my heart race.

57
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,100
The one who made me
stop fearing physical touch.

58
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,000
The one I fell in love with.

59
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,600
The one who made you question...

60
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,400
what's real and what isn't.

61
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:19,790
But my feelings for her are real, Doc.

62
00:04:21,090 --> 00:04:22,090
Then...

63
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:23,220
don't be afraid of the truth.

64
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:27,110
Can you put it more simply?

65
00:04:30,030 --> 00:04:31,370
Just tell me

66
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,600
what's stressing you out

67
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,300
so I can give you the right advice.

68
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,260
We won't get anywhere

69
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,690
if you keep beating around the bush.

70
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,320
My girlfriend dreamed

71
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:42,700
and apologized to me in her sleep.

72
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:45,400
So I asked her why...

73
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,700
I'm sorry, Chris...

74
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:52,610
for not taking good care of myself.

75
00:04:53,890 --> 00:04:56,100
I made you worry about me.

76
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:00,400
No,

77
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,800
it's my fault.

78
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,390
This is my fault.

79
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,900
How is that your fault?

80
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,450
I was still worried about Nadear,

81
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:17,770
so I couldn't properly take care of Sun.

82
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:20,010
And...

83
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,550
what are you worried about with Nadear?

84
00:05:22,430 --> 00:05:23,910
It used to be about Nan.

85
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,200
But now I need to think it over.

86
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:27,950
Because

87
00:05:27,970 --> 00:05:30,710
Nan might not be Nadear's
enemy as I thought.

88
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:33,000
The easiest thing to do

89
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:34,310
is distance yourself.

90
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:44,880
You've come this far already.

91
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,440
When are you gonna tell Chris?

92
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:48,610
Or are you gonna let
Nadear tell her herself?

93
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:52,640
Didn't you say sleeping with her
would make you more confident?

94
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,590
I was wrong.

95
00:05:55,610 --> 00:05:57,000
After we slept together...

96
00:05:57,590 --> 00:05:59,320
I'm even more afraid of losing her again.

97
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,090
Then choose

98
00:06:02,110 --> 00:06:04,460
whether you want to let Nadear tell her herself,

99
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,520
so she can spin the story however she wants,

100
00:06:06,550 --> 00:06:08,120
or let Chris find out on her own

101
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:09,890
and come up with all sorts of wrong ideas.

102
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,760
Or are you gonna hide it from her forever?

103
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,590
It wouldn't be hard to convince her
since she loves you so much.

104
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,590
Chris!

105
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,100
You're in my room.

106
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:34,610
Sun...

107
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:41,800
You're right.

108
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,500
If I don't tell her the truth,

109
00:06:46,150 --> 00:06:47,910
I'd be no different from Nadear.

110
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,690
Chris will never be happy.

111
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,880
Stop sulking, then.

112
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:58,280
Get up, take a shower,
and get to work already.

113
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,570
And tonight,

114
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:01,510
tell her the truth.

115
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,610
Lie down and talk.

116
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:06,100
Things will slowly get better that way, yeah?

117
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:07,800
Mm.

118
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:10,290
Thanks.

119
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:10,910
Mm.

120
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:11,730
I'm gonna go shower.

121
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:12,900
Yeah, about time.

122
00:07:13,210 --> 00:07:14,210
I can smell you from here.

123
00:07:14,890 --> 00:07:15,990
Come on, get up.

124
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,900
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

125
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:26,440
You'd like to withdraw
Ms. Nan's shares, correct?

126
00:07:26,770 --> 00:07:27,490
No,

127
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,160
I'd like to withdraw mine.

128
00:07:29,590 --> 00:07:30,960
What are you doing?

129
00:07:36,670 --> 00:07:37,690
Answer me!

130
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:40,500
Have you gotten better?

131
00:07:41,410 --> 00:07:42,810
You still care?

132
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:44,610
No,

133
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,920
I just want to know
what you'll come up with this time.

134
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:52,310
I already know
you've been hurting yourself.

135
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:56,800
And now I know why you let Nan
keep embezzling money from our restaurant.

136
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:01,310
If you enjoy playing the victim,

137
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,900
then don't try to make me
the villain, Nadear.

138
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,200
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

139
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:19,440
Are you really going to leave
this restaurant?

140
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:25,520
To be honest... I'm not that useful
to this restaurant.

141
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,600
That's not true.

142
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,040
I've seen how hard you've worked.

143
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,090
I wasn't here when
this restaurant first opened,

144
00:08:33,110 --> 00:08:34,710
but didn't the restaurant's name...

145
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:37,700
come from the three of you?

146
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,960
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

147
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:52,200
'Third Person' might not be
what the name suggests anymore.

148
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,900
Maybe the number three is unlucky.

149
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,100
I've thought it through.

150
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,510
The restaurant should belong to Nadear.

151
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:03,190
No,

152
00:09:04,590 --> 00:09:06,310
if you're not here,

153
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,400
Nan might treat Nadear even worse.

154
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:14,510
Or maybe...

155
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:18,370
Nan might have nothing left
to use against Nadear now.

156
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:21,300
Wawah,

157
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,400
I trust you the most.

158
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:27,520
Please take care of Nadear for me.

159
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,440
[Closed]

160
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:09,890
Why did you steal money
from the restaurant?

161
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,680
I thought you were here because
I hurt your girlfriend.

162
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,430
You and Nadear are allies, aren't you?

163
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:17,190
No,

164
00:10:17,690 --> 00:10:19,190
I'm my own ally.

165
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:22,390
Good.

166
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:26,600
What do I have to do for you
to tell me the truth?

167
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:28,400
What are you planning?

168
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:34,880
I'm selling my shares in the restaurant.

169
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:36,810
You want them?

170
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:41,110
You could get more than you stole.

171
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,530
Why did you ring the doorbell?

172
00:10:57,550 --> 00:10:59,170
You have the keycard, don't you?

173
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,210
I wanted to ask properly first.

174
00:11:03,710 --> 00:11:06,700
I might be troubling you for
more than just one night this time.

175
00:11:11,730 --> 00:11:13,790
You can trouble me forever.

176
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:29,510
Mm...

177
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:31,090
This looks delicious.

178
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:34,700
I bought it from the place near my clinic.

179
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,110
Give it a try.

180
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:39,690
That way, when a customer asks,
you can recommend something.

181
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:43,390
Oh, wow...

182
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:46,190
From what I just heard,

183
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:49,840
you're not romantic at all, Doc.

184
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:56,730
Is it really okay to celebrate today?

185
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:01,580
You just went through something
uncomfortable, didn't you?

186
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:14,990
It's something I should've done a while ago.

187
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:18,100
If we're going to live together,

188
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,600
we should talk things through like this.

189
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,310
It's pretty realistic.

190
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,000
I'm a pro at buying cheap food.

191
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,280
Work keeps me busy enough already.

192
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,080
Mm.

193
00:12:34,010 --> 00:12:36,120
That sounds nice.

194
00:12:38,110 --> 00:12:39,110
How?

195
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:44,000
How we're going to live together from now on.

196
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,920
Chris...

197
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,100
I have to work at the clinic

198
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,190
to pay back the debt I owe my father.

199
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,310
I don't have anything I can call my own.

200
00:13:08,110 --> 00:13:09,310
Whether it's a house

201
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,510
or a car.

202
00:13:15,210 --> 00:13:17,400
My father spent so much money

203
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,400
sending me abroad for treatment.

204
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:27,510
You were sent abroad for treatment?

205
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:30,700
Chris...

206
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,380
The truth is...

207
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:50,280
Sun...

208
00:13:50,590 --> 00:13:51,200
Sun.

209
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:53,510
Sun? What's wrong?

210
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:55,810
Sun?

211
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:57,910
Are you alright?

212
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:00,980
Sun, are you okay?

213
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:06,300
[Third Person]

214
00:14:08,364 --> 00:14:11,344
[Third Person]

215
00:14:27,044 --> 00:14:28,734
Are you sure you're alright?

216
00:14:30,134 --> 00:14:31,554
Shouldn't you go see a doctor?

217
00:14:33,304 --> 00:14:34,644
Chris, I'm a doctor.

218
00:14:36,264 --> 00:14:37,834
I know I'll be fine.

219
00:14:41,094 --> 00:14:42,754
But I'm your girlfriend,

220
00:14:43,324 --> 00:14:44,544
and I don't know that.

221
00:14:45,024 --> 00:14:46,224
I'm worried about you.

222
00:14:55,734 --> 00:14:56,984
I'll be alright.

223
00:14:57,554 --> 00:14:58,554
Really?

224
00:15:00,124 --> 00:15:00,734
Mm.

225
00:15:01,854 --> 00:15:03,044
It's just a migraine.

226
00:15:04,034 --> 00:15:05,524
The clinic just opened.

227
00:15:05,974 --> 00:15:07,054
There's so much to do.

228
00:15:09,154 --> 00:15:10,154
Then...

229
00:15:10,914 --> 00:15:12,264
can you try not to stress so much?

230
00:15:13,334 --> 00:15:15,174
Or at least share it with me

231
00:15:15,194 --> 00:15:16,494
when you are stressed?

232
00:15:18,444 --> 00:15:20,624
You can tell me anything.

233
00:15:24,744 --> 00:15:25,704
Yes, babe.

234
00:15:27,034 --> 00:15:29,144
First things first, take a shower.

235
00:15:31,994 --> 00:15:32,854
What about you, Sun?

236
00:15:34,234 --> 00:15:35,654
Go on ahead.

237
00:15:41,554 --> 00:15:42,534
Alright,

238
00:15:46,044 --> 00:15:48,554
I'll help you relax.

239
00:15:53,404 --> 00:15:54,434
Chris?

240
00:15:58,204 --> 00:15:59,484
What are you doing?

241
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,334
Chris!

242
00:16:16,454 --> 00:16:19,344
That headache came back.

243
00:16:19,744 --> 00:16:21,984
[That headache came back]

244
00:16:28,104 --> 00:16:29,284
Your medical history shows

245
00:16:29,304 --> 00:16:33,044
that you had a tumor near the brainstem.

246
00:16:33,744 --> 00:16:36,374
Tumors near the brainstem

247
00:16:36,394 --> 00:16:38,744
are at high risk of recurring.

248
00:16:38,944 --> 00:16:40,534
It's a good thing you came in early.

249
00:16:43,244 --> 00:16:45,444
Will it come back?

250
00:16:46,374 --> 00:16:48,534
I can't say for sure yet.

251
00:16:48,564 --> 00:16:50,864
I need to examine you thoroughly first.

252
00:17:08,384 --> 00:17:10,704
Chris, you're back?

253
00:17:18,644 --> 00:17:19,644
Dr. Jeen.

254
00:17:20,804 --> 00:17:21,844
Jeen.

255
00:17:22,944 --> 00:17:24,164
Call me Jeen.

256
00:17:25,344 --> 00:17:26,754
It doesn't matter what I call you.

257
00:17:34,644 --> 00:17:35,434
It does.

258
00:17:37,354 --> 00:17:38,744
I'm not just a doctor.

259
00:17:41,064 --> 00:17:42,554
I'm yours, Nadear.

260
00:17:47,944 --> 00:17:48,944
Why are you here?

261
00:17:53,264 --> 00:17:54,534
Chris already left.

262
00:17:56,404 --> 00:17:57,744
I came to see you.

263
00:17:58,744 --> 00:18:00,244
Chris already left,

264
00:18:00,864 --> 00:18:02,204
but you're still here.

265
00:18:03,734 --> 00:18:05,224
You have to keep going.

266
00:18:08,824 --> 00:18:11,254
Are you here to see if I'm dead yet?

267
00:18:15,154 --> 00:18:16,464
If I am,

268
00:18:17,044 --> 00:18:19,164
just know it was your fault.

269
00:18:19,664 --> 00:18:22,464
Because you're stupid and
can't do anything right.

270
00:18:23,264 --> 00:18:25,454
You made her leave me!

271
00:18:26,494 --> 00:18:28,634
I have no one left.

272
00:18:46,624 --> 00:18:48,424
You can say whatever you want to me,

273
00:18:51,564 --> 00:18:52,644
but don't say

274
00:18:54,644 --> 00:18:56,064
that you have no one left.

275
00:19:18,834 --> 00:19:20,454
It might take some time,

276
00:19:21,334 --> 00:19:22,544
but things will get better.

277
00:19:24,694 --> 00:19:25,924
Thank you, Doc.

278
00:19:28,154 --> 00:19:30,864
I can rest easy with you by her side.

279
00:19:33,124 --> 00:19:33,864
Yeah.

280
00:19:35,314 --> 00:19:36,524
I...

281
00:19:36,544 --> 00:19:38,044
should have realized sooner.

282
00:19:39,674 --> 00:19:40,734
What do you mean?

283
00:19:41,594 --> 00:19:42,324
It's nothing.

284
00:19:43,554 --> 00:19:44,664
Like I said before,

285
00:19:45,394 --> 00:19:47,184
you can't help how you feel.

286
00:19:48,344 --> 00:19:50,384
If you're going to leave Nadear,

287
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:52,444
don't ever go back to her.

288
00:19:53,564 --> 00:19:55,984
Don't give her hope again.

289
00:19:57,554 --> 00:19:58,714
And...

290
00:19:59,024 --> 00:20:00,334
you don't have to worry about her.

291
00:20:02,674 --> 00:20:04,184
I can take care of her.

292
00:20:05,444 --> 00:20:06,704
The truth is...

293
00:20:08,144 --> 00:20:09,644
I've always taken care of Nadear.

294
00:20:11,604 --> 00:20:13,864
You're the best friend I've ever had.

295
00:20:24,154 --> 00:20:24,964
I'll get going now.

296
00:20:25,264 --> 00:20:25,844
Mm.

297
00:20:33,944 --> 00:20:35,154
I'm sorry, Chris.

298
00:20:37,244 --> 00:20:39,334
I couldn't even bring myself to tell you

299
00:20:41,364 --> 00:20:42,824
that this is my fault.

300
00:21:01,124 --> 00:21:02,024
Nadear!

301
00:21:23,464 --> 00:21:28,024
[Craniopharyngioma]

302
00:21:54,524 --> 00:21:56,444
Babe.

303
00:21:56,814 --> 00:21:57,554
Hey,

304
00:21:58,544 --> 00:21:59,844
I brought this for you.

305
00:22:05,854 --> 00:22:07,434
Dust can trigger migraines, right?

306
00:22:07,454 --> 00:22:09,324
That's why I brought you this
air-purifying plant.

307
00:22:09,344 --> 00:22:11,034
You can keep it indoors,

308
00:22:11,054 --> 00:22:13,264
and it helps purify the air.

309
00:22:16,154 --> 00:22:17,744
You're the best.

310
00:22:18,544 --> 00:22:19,584
Right?

311
00:22:19,924 --> 00:22:22,584
You won't find a girlfriend like me
anywhere else.

312
00:22:40,464 --> 00:22:41,324
Yeah.

313
00:22:42,254 --> 00:22:43,944
Nowhere else.

314
00:22:53,254 --> 00:22:54,344
What's wrong?

315
00:22:55,814 --> 00:22:57,354
Are you stressed about the clinic?

316
00:23:03,224 --> 00:23:05,564
I'm planning to sell Nadear
my shares in the restaurant.

317
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:06,944
I should get a decent amount for them.

318
00:23:07,654 --> 00:23:09,784
If you need more money, just tell me.

319
00:23:11,364 --> 00:23:13,584
But don't stress yourself out
or get sick again, okay?

320
00:23:21,444 --> 00:23:23,054
I'm fine.

321
00:23:24,544 --> 00:23:25,644
I'm not sick.

322
00:23:26,744 --> 00:23:28,234
I'm staying here with you.

323
00:23:32,504 --> 00:23:34,024
Aw...

324
00:23:34,424 --> 00:23:36,054
You're so stressed out, aren't you?

325
00:23:37,754 --> 00:23:39,464
It's okay.

326
00:23:41,354 --> 00:23:42,184
How about this?

327
00:23:44,164 --> 00:23:45,554
Let's go to the flower farm tomorrow.

328
00:23:48,144 --> 00:23:48,824
Yeah.

329
00:24:28,774 --> 00:24:30,784
Aw...

330
00:24:33,174 --> 00:24:34,444
Don't be sad.

331
00:24:34,954 --> 00:24:36,064
I'm the one who's sick,

332
00:24:36,334 --> 00:24:37,984
not you.

333
00:24:38,524 --> 00:24:39,454
But...

334
00:24:39,474 --> 00:24:40,734
how can you be so calm?

335
00:24:42,064 --> 00:24:43,344
I'm not.

336
00:24:44,554 --> 00:24:46,824
But the doctor did say it could come back.

337
00:24:48,914 --> 00:24:51,304
Can you act a little sadder?

338
00:24:51,954 --> 00:24:52,844
Nope.

339
00:24:54,594 --> 00:24:56,244
If it comes back,
I have to get treatment.

340
00:24:56,594 --> 00:24:57,904
I have to get better.

341
00:25:00,134 --> 00:25:02,144
I won't lose Chris again.

342
00:25:02,754 --> 00:25:04,254
What if you forget everything again?

343
00:25:05,434 --> 00:25:06,844
I've forgotten before.

344
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:09,064
Chris has, too.

345
00:25:10,034 --> 00:25:12,444
Some memories might fade.

346
00:25:13,944 --> 00:25:15,784
But if the feelings are still there,

347
00:25:17,344 --> 00:25:18,584
I believe...

348
00:25:19,424 --> 00:25:20,744
as long as we still love each other,

349
00:25:21,244 --> 00:25:22,644
we'll always love each other.

350
00:25:28,174 --> 00:25:30,244
And now I have you here.

351
00:25:31,734 --> 00:25:33,034
If I forget again,

352
00:25:34,154 --> 00:25:36,654
you'll take me to Chris, right?

353
00:25:36,674 --> 00:25:38,514
- Mm...
- Right?

354
00:25:38,544 --> 00:25:40,084
Sure,

355
00:25:40,104 --> 00:25:41,044
smarty.

356
00:25:41,544 --> 00:25:42,624
But first things first,

357
00:25:43,004 --> 00:25:45,264
you have to tell Chris the truth

358
00:25:45,564 --> 00:25:47,584
before you forget again.

359
00:25:48,864 --> 00:25:50,544
Yes, Mom.

360
00:25:51,344 --> 00:25:52,824
You've got this, my girl.

361
00:25:56,644 --> 00:25:57,644
Chris,

362
00:25:58,624 --> 00:26:00,734
I won't make the same mistake again.

363
00:26:09,054 --> 00:26:10,054
Yes, Jeen?

364
00:26:27,654 --> 00:26:28,334
Sun!

365
00:26:31,874 --> 00:26:32,584
Sun.

366
00:26:32,604 --> 00:26:33,534
Sun.

367
00:26:34,314 --> 00:26:34,954
Sun.

368
00:26:39,254 --> 00:26:43,154
[Third Person]

369
00:26:44,424 --> 00:26:48,194
[Third Person]

370
00:26:49,954 --> 00:26:51,754
You were stressed and hadn't eaten,

371
00:26:51,774 --> 00:26:52,774
and your blood pressure dropped.

372
00:26:53,384 --> 00:26:54,664
Why didn't you tell me?

373
00:26:56,764 --> 00:26:57,764
I was excited

374
00:27:00,214 --> 00:27:01,634
about going to the flower farm.

375
00:27:02,334 --> 00:27:03,664
And we had to cut the trip short.

376
00:27:03,684 --> 00:27:04,724
Isn't that great, huh?

377
00:27:05,304 --> 00:27:06,694
Can you take me there again?

378
00:27:10,334 --> 00:27:11,594
Eat first.

379
00:27:17,114 --> 00:27:18,234
I'll take you there tomorrow.

380
00:27:26,904 --> 00:27:28,204
You stubborn girl.

381
00:27:30,704 --> 00:27:31,994
Will you still love me, then?

382
00:27:33,794 --> 00:27:36,604
I won't if you don't take care of yourself.

383
00:27:44,084 --> 00:27:45,474
One more bite.

384
00:27:54,984 --> 00:27:55,694
Sun,

385
00:27:56,754 --> 00:27:58,014
I have something to tell you.

386
00:27:59,304 --> 00:28:01,324
But don't worry too much, okay?

387
00:28:03,374 --> 00:28:04,984
How can I not worry

388
00:28:05,444 --> 00:28:06,894
when you start by saying that?

389
00:28:08,494 --> 00:28:09,574
Nadear tried to kill herself...

390
00:28:10,394 --> 00:28:11,074
Huh...?

391
00:28:11,494 --> 00:28:13,284
But I'm not going back to her.

392
00:28:15,214 --> 00:28:18,804
I know Nadear might use this
to make me stay with her.

393
00:28:22,644 --> 00:28:25,194
I'm just going to see
the doctor who treated me.

394
00:28:26,194 --> 00:28:28,084
She's taking care of Nadear now.

395
00:28:30,754 --> 00:28:32,274
What about you? Are you alright?

396
00:28:41,794 --> 00:28:43,504
I think it's partly my fault.

397
00:28:45,184 --> 00:28:47,894
I always gave Nadear what she wanted,

398
00:28:48,734 --> 00:28:50,944
and I think that pushed her to this point.

399
00:28:53,584 --> 00:28:55,774
I want to help you, too.

400
00:29:08,584 --> 00:29:10,494
As long as you're healthy,
that's enough for me.

401
00:29:11,794 --> 00:29:14,784
Just having you in this world
already helps me so much.

402
00:29:18,074 --> 00:29:19,704
I'll live for you, Chris.

403
00:30:12,724 --> 00:30:13,494
Nadear!

404
00:30:14,414 --> 00:30:15,194
Nadear?!

405
00:30:16,614 --> 00:30:17,364
Nadear!

406
00:30:17,894 --> 00:30:19,394
Leave me alone!

407
00:30:19,704 --> 00:30:21,614
You betrayed me!

408
00:30:21,644 --> 00:30:23,604
Nadear, I'm sorry!

409
00:30:24,534 --> 00:30:25,694
I'll do it...

410
00:30:28,054 --> 00:30:30,194
I'll make Chris yours again.

411
00:30:31,014 --> 00:30:32,304
I'm sorry...

412
00:30:32,884 --> 00:30:34,194
I'll do it for you, Nadear.

413
00:30:36,324 --> 00:30:37,024
Nadear...

414
00:30:37,414 --> 00:30:39,594
Nadear, Nadear... Nadear!

415
00:30:39,844 --> 00:30:40,784
Nadear!

416
00:31:05,554 --> 00:31:07,094
What happened to Nadear, Doc?

417
00:31:08,494 --> 00:31:10,304
Nadear is really upset over losing you.

418
00:31:11,104 --> 00:31:12,804
So I told her

419
00:31:12,824 --> 00:31:14,274
I'd help you regain your memories

420
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:16,014
so this could finally end.

421
00:31:17,124 --> 00:31:18,284
But she wouldn't accept that,

422
00:31:19,304 --> 00:31:20,304
so she acted out of spite.

423
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:25,094
Help me remember?

424
00:31:26,694 --> 00:31:27,694
What do you mean?

425
00:31:32,104 --> 00:31:32,794
Chris,

426
00:31:33,604 --> 00:31:34,604
I'm sorry.

427
00:31:36,434 --> 00:31:38,194
The hypnosis I performed on you

428
00:31:38,624 --> 00:31:40,394
wasn't meant to help you remember,

429
00:31:41,164 --> 00:31:42,504
but to make you forget.

430
00:31:50,634 --> 00:31:51,694
Why...?

431
00:31:56,204 --> 00:31:58,294
Because if you knew the truth,

432
00:32:00,214 --> 00:32:02,194
you might not be able to stay with Nadear.

433
00:32:03,564 --> 00:32:04,404
And...

434
00:32:05,614 --> 00:32:07,714
Nadear can't lose you, either.

435
00:32:08,404 --> 00:32:09,704
What truth?

436
00:32:13,204 --> 00:32:14,814
The truth between you and Sun.

437
00:32:26,384 --> 00:32:28,104
I'll have to...

438
00:32:28,134 --> 00:32:29,494
tell you the truth,

439
00:32:30,694 --> 00:32:32,504
because I don't know what to do anymore.

440
00:32:34,984 --> 00:32:36,694
Do you still want to know the truth?

441
00:32:38,614 --> 00:32:40,014
The truth.

442
00:32:42,764 --> 00:32:45,784
You mean my real memories?

443
00:33:15,304 --> 00:33:16,614
She still hasn't answered?

444
00:33:20,594 --> 00:33:24,504
Are you going to have surgery here,
or go back to your previous doctor?

445
00:33:30,694 --> 00:33:31,694
I'll have surgery here.

446
00:33:33,994 --> 00:33:35,394
I have to get better,

447
00:33:37,094 --> 00:33:38,784
and remember everything, too.

448
00:34:12,814 --> 00:34:13,704
Sun,

449
00:34:16,294 --> 00:34:18,804
that girl with dark hair.

450
00:34:20,054 --> 00:34:21,594
She's quiet and reserved.

451
00:34:23,304 --> 00:34:25,804
She was your only close friend

452
00:34:26,144 --> 00:34:27,474
in middle school.

453
00:34:44,804 --> 00:34:45,594
Sun

454
00:34:46,924 --> 00:34:47,994
was your

455
00:34:48,014 --> 00:34:50,074
most important friend.

456
00:34:51,614 --> 00:34:52,904
Until...

457
00:34:53,574 --> 00:34:54,574
Nadear

458
00:34:55,164 --> 00:34:56,714
came along and became your new friend.

459
00:35:00,004 --> 00:35:00,594
Here.

460
00:35:08,094 --> 00:35:09,094
Hey, wait!

461
00:35:09,804 --> 00:35:10,514
Chris!

462
00:35:48,584 --> 00:35:50,504
Who...is Sun?

463
00:35:55,004 --> 00:35:55,914
My best friend.

464
00:35:56,444 --> 00:35:57,394
That's right.

465
00:35:59,094 --> 00:36:00,154
Sun...

466
00:36:01,424 --> 00:36:02,594
is your best friend

467
00:36:03,434 --> 00:36:05,494
who's been secretly in love with you all along.

468
00:36:43,594 --> 00:36:45,574
I love the smell of your shampoo.

469
00:36:48,674 --> 00:36:50,884
Hey, it's okay now,

470
00:36:50,904 --> 00:36:52,304
my dear.

471
00:37:27,984 --> 00:37:29,754
Is Nadear alright?

472
00:37:42,594 --> 00:37:44,784
The doctors are keeping a close eye on her.

473
00:37:49,944 --> 00:37:51,004
What about you?

474
00:37:52,594 --> 00:37:53,594
Are you alright?

475
00:37:55,964 --> 00:37:57,704
Are you feeling any better?

476
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:01,704
Seeing a friend in that state

477
00:38:02,324 --> 00:38:04,294
must have been really upsetting.

478
00:38:14,894 --> 00:38:16,904
Why do you know me so well?

479
00:38:19,084 --> 00:38:20,214
Of course I do.

480
00:38:21,434 --> 00:38:22,694
The Chris I love

481
00:38:23,214 --> 00:38:25,994
always puts others before herself.

482
00:38:30,104 --> 00:38:31,784
What about the Sun I love?

483
00:38:34,104 --> 00:38:35,494
I'm yours.

484
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:52,884
You smell nicer than the roses.

485
00:38:57,684 --> 00:38:59,014
You smell even better.

486
00:39:02,194 --> 00:39:03,704
Have you gotten better?

487
00:39:03,794 --> 00:39:05,024
Getting all feisty like this.

488
00:39:06,204 --> 00:39:07,594
I feel better now.

489
00:39:10,334 --> 00:39:11,334
Then...

490
00:39:11,354 --> 00:39:12,184
Let's go.

491
00:39:13,514 --> 00:39:14,414
Where to?

492
00:39:15,814 --> 00:39:17,494
To pay for the damages.

493
00:39:18,104 --> 00:39:19,964
You fell on a bunch of flowers

494
00:39:19,994 --> 00:39:22,164
and crushed so many of them last time.

495
00:39:22,924 --> 00:39:23,904
Chris!

496
00:39:24,434 --> 00:39:25,814
Just kidding.

497
00:39:26,494 --> 00:39:29,004
You said you wanted to go to
the flower farm, after all.

498
00:39:29,594 --> 00:39:30,884
Let's go, then.

499
00:39:33,064 --> 00:39:33,804
Yes,

500
00:39:37,824 --> 00:39:39,804
I want to go everywhere with you.

501
00:39:41,204 --> 00:39:43,474
Whether it's somewhere we've been,
somewhere new,

502
00:39:44,204 --> 00:39:45,894
or the same place over and over.

503
00:39:46,904 --> 00:39:48,914
As long as you're there with me.

504
00:39:51,704 --> 00:39:52,814
Of course,

505
00:39:52,844 --> 00:39:54,594
I'll go everywhere with you.

506
00:40:23,694 --> 00:40:27,794
[Third Person]

507
00:40:29,340 --> 00:40:32,830
[Third Person]

508
00:40:46,420 --> 00:40:47,710
Jeen...

509
00:40:49,820 --> 00:40:51,440
It's alright now, Nadear.

510
00:40:58,320 --> 00:40:59,720
Promise...

511
00:41:02,050 --> 00:41:03,330
Don't worry.

512
00:41:04,050 --> 00:41:05,820
I did what you asked.

513
00:41:21,150 --> 00:41:22,140
Did you know?

514
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:24,140
Going everywhere with you

515
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:25,830
has always been my dream.

516
00:41:27,900 --> 00:41:29,020
You love going out, huh?

517
00:41:30,140 --> 00:41:31,830
I just like traveling.

518
00:41:33,820 --> 00:41:34,700
Why?

519
00:41:36,420 --> 00:41:39,030
Maybe because it feels endless.

520
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:41,520
Especially

521
00:41:41,540 --> 00:41:43,410
now that we're really together.

522
00:41:44,630 --> 00:41:48,840
It feels like this moment is truly ours.

523
00:41:51,520 --> 00:41:54,200
But if you faint again,
I won't take you there anymore.

524
00:41:57,750 --> 00:41:59,140
If I faint again,

525
00:41:59,870 --> 00:42:01,400
I probably won't get to go anymore.

526
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,440
That's odd.

527
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:05,710
Is something wrong?

528
00:42:07,070 --> 00:42:08,240
It's nothing.

529
00:42:08,620 --> 00:42:09,620
I mean...

530
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:12,410
you won't take me there anymore, right?

531
00:42:27,790 --> 00:42:28,790
There you are.

532
00:42:30,520 --> 00:42:31,430
What's on your mind?

533
00:42:33,010 --> 00:42:35,230
Last time, I fainted among the flowers.

534
00:42:36,060 --> 00:42:37,830
Not exactly the best of memory.

535
00:42:39,040 --> 00:42:41,890
I don't want you to
remember me that way.

536
00:42:42,820 --> 00:42:45,430
But every moment we spent together,

537
00:42:46,790 --> 00:42:48,820
either good or bad,

538
00:42:50,220 --> 00:42:52,130
I'll always cherish them.

539
00:42:53,260 --> 00:42:54,600
I have something for you.

540
00:42:58,570 --> 00:42:59,300
Rose.

541
00:43:00,380 --> 00:43:01,810
The flower that brought us together.

542
00:43:09,130 --> 00:43:09,850
Here.

543
00:43:20,830 --> 00:43:22,310
Thank you so much, Sun.

544
00:43:25,350 --> 00:43:27,260
I have something to tell you.

545
00:43:28,620 --> 00:43:29,810
I...

546
00:43:29,830 --> 00:43:30,910
I already knew that.

547
00:43:41,430 --> 00:43:42,430
Where is Chris?

548
00:43:43,440 --> 00:43:45,150
I told her to go.

549
00:43:45,810 --> 00:43:46,900
Where to?

550
00:43:47,620 --> 00:43:48,720
To settle things

551
00:43:49,220 --> 00:43:50,400
one last time.

552
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:53,820
Are you tricking me again?

553
00:43:54,670 --> 00:43:55,720
You know full well

554
00:43:56,350 --> 00:43:58,620
what I'm most afraid of.

555
00:44:01,730 --> 00:44:03,540
I love you, Jeen.

556
00:44:21,250 --> 00:44:22,130
You...?

557
00:44:23,140 --> 00:44:23,900
Nan?

558
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:26,860
That's right!

559
00:44:27,240 --> 00:44:28,730
Didn't you say you'd drop it?!

560
00:44:30,140 --> 00:44:32,210
Then what's this police summons
doing at my house?!

561
00:44:32,230 --> 00:44:33,450
Stop... Stop!

562
00:44:34,950 --> 00:44:37,420
You want me to tell Chris the truth, right?

563
00:44:37,710 --> 00:44:39,700
Stop threatening me with Chris.

564
00:44:41,440 --> 00:44:42,120
Why?

565
00:44:42,630 --> 00:44:44,340
Got yourself a new partner?

566
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:46,320
If the summons is taking too long,

567
00:44:46,720 --> 00:44:50,050
why not spend a night in jail
for trespassing instead?

568
00:44:50,150 --> 00:44:50,970
Nadear!

569
00:44:53,920 --> 00:44:55,140
The money you embezzled

570
00:44:55,160 --> 00:44:57,380
should be more than enough
for you to live in luxury.

571
00:44:57,630 --> 00:44:59,000
I reported you to the police

572
00:44:59,020 --> 00:45:01,980
because you're greedy,
stupid, and useless.

573
00:45:02,520 --> 00:45:04,420
If you'd kept quiet and done nothing,

574
00:45:05,310 --> 00:45:07,420
would Chris have left me?!

575
00:45:08,110 --> 00:45:09,620
Stop acting all innocent.

576
00:45:13,740 --> 00:45:16,320
See what I've had to go through

577
00:45:16,340 --> 00:45:17,690
because you didn't do enough to help me?

578
00:45:30,830 --> 00:45:32,220
What are you to that crazy bitch?

579
00:45:33,970 --> 00:45:37,010
I won't let anyone harm Nadear.

580
00:45:37,320 --> 00:45:39,210
I'll prove it by...

581
00:45:39,630 --> 00:45:41,630
If you don't leave this house right away,

582
00:45:42,230 --> 00:45:43,310
I'm calling the police.

583
00:46:01,580 --> 00:46:03,010
Chris, I'm sorry.

584
00:46:03,620 --> 00:46:05,810
It's too late for me to turn back now.

585
00:46:08,330 --> 00:46:09,430
What did you know?

586
00:46:12,130 --> 00:46:14,010
I remember who you were.

587
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:21,710
Here.

588
00:46:21,930 --> 00:46:23,410
She gave it to me

589
00:46:23,430 --> 00:46:25,530
before Buddhism class.

590
00:46:35,570 --> 00:46:36,500
Hey, wait!

591
00:46:37,220 --> 00:46:37,980
Chris!

592
00:46:45,010 --> 00:46:46,710
Have you finished copying my homework?

593
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:49,150
Not yet. Are you going to turn it in now?

594
00:46:49,710 --> 00:46:50,470
It's alright.

595
00:46:50,490 --> 00:46:51,520
I'll wait until you're done.

596
00:46:52,550 --> 00:46:53,500
Give me a sec.

597
00:46:58,730 --> 00:46:59,730
Chris...

598
00:47:03,650 --> 00:47:04,800
It's alright now.

599
00:47:12,730 --> 00:47:14,220
My parents...

600
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:18,910
they're gone.

601
00:47:29,530 --> 00:47:33,220
I feel like Sun got my dog
killed on purpose.

602
00:47:34,620 --> 00:47:37,320
Sun isn't heartless, Nadear.

603
00:47:38,240 --> 00:47:39,430
You know that.

604
00:47:39,450 --> 00:47:40,800
She's my friend.

605
00:47:41,430 --> 00:47:43,570
A friend who secretly loves you?

606
00:47:47,140 --> 00:47:48,140
Nadear...

607
00:47:53,240 --> 00:47:54,710
Did you and Nadear fight again?

608
00:47:55,520 --> 00:47:56,210
Mm.

609
00:47:57,340 --> 00:47:59,110
Nadear never understands me.

610
00:48:00,420 --> 00:48:01,940
What is it this time?

611
00:48:05,150 --> 00:48:06,220
It's about you.

612
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:09,430
A girlfriend and a best friend.

613
00:48:09,910 --> 00:48:10,910
It's nothing new.

614
00:48:17,270 --> 00:48:18,700
Nadear told me you love me.

615
00:48:19,340 --> 00:48:20,610
How could that be?

616
00:48:21,260 --> 00:48:23,120
We've known each other since middle school.

617
00:48:35,820 --> 00:48:36,820
Right...

618
00:48:37,520 --> 00:48:39,510
We've known each other since middle school.

619
00:48:40,520 --> 00:48:42,420
So if you're going to love someone,

620
00:48:43,310 --> 00:48:44,510
why can't it be me?

621
00:49:04,330 --> 00:49:05,330
Chris,

622
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:07,100
I'm sorry...

623
00:49:07,630 --> 00:49:10,010
I thought I already closed the door.

624
00:49:10,530 --> 00:49:12,380
I didn't think that Nadear would see us.

625
00:49:13,020 --> 00:49:13,920
Forget it.

626
00:49:14,110 --> 00:49:16,340
Right now, we have to find Nadear.

627
00:49:16,510 --> 00:49:17,820
She was furious.

628
00:49:18,430 --> 00:49:19,980
I can't lose her.

629
00:49:22,390 --> 00:49:23,710
If you still love her,

630
00:49:25,020 --> 00:49:26,530
then why are you with me?

631
00:49:28,940 --> 00:49:30,220
I'm sorry, Sun.

632
00:49:30,770 --> 00:49:31,820
But I love Nadear.

633
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:42,000
Nadear doesn't want me to remember,

634
00:49:43,040 --> 00:49:44,540
so I won't have to feel guilty.

635
00:49:45,620 --> 00:49:48,730
But she probably didn't think
I'd make the same mistake twice.

636
00:49:49,630 --> 00:49:50,710
No...

637
00:49:52,220 --> 00:49:53,410
I know

638
00:49:54,210 --> 00:49:56,120
why you apologized to me now.

639
00:49:57,920 --> 00:49:59,430
That's not it, Chris.

640
00:50:00,130 --> 00:50:01,900
We both betrayed Nadear.

641
00:50:03,050 --> 00:50:05,700
We made her this way.

642
00:50:08,040 --> 00:50:09,540
I do love you,

643
00:50:12,860 --> 00:50:15,340
but our relationship was wrong
from the beginning.

644
00:50:23,010 --> 00:50:26,860
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image,♫

645
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:30,600
♫Yet the love that never faded♫

646
00:50:30,620 --> 00:50:33,650
♫Like a missing page♫

647
00:50:33,670 --> 00:50:37,070
♫I can't find♫

648
00:50:37,090 --> 00:50:40,180
♫Your smell lingers vividly in my mind♫

649
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:44,830
Stop talking,

650
00:50:45,040 --> 00:50:46,100
and listen to me.

651
00:50:46,920 --> 00:50:50,390
♫You're still so clear in my heart♫

652
00:50:50,410 --> 00:50:54,290
♫But who are you?♫

653
00:50:54,310 --> 00:50:57,370
♫...Please tell me♫

654
00:50:57,440 --> 00:50:59,660
I won't let Chris stay with Nadear anymore.

655
00:50:59,710 --> 00:51:01,180
I have to save her.

656
00:51:01,630 --> 00:51:02,780
I promise

657
00:51:02,930 --> 00:51:04,420
I won't make the same mistake again.

658
00:51:04,440 --> 00:51:05,550
From now on,

659
00:51:05,570 --> 00:51:07,530
there will be just the two of us.

660
00:51:07,550 --> 00:51:09,500
I'm living

661
00:51:09,540 --> 00:51:11,200
for you right now, Jeen.

662
00:51:11,220 --> 00:51:13,230
I want to end this, too.

663
00:51:13,580 --> 00:51:15,610
But you have to remember

664
00:51:15,630 --> 00:51:17,990
what really happened on your own.

665
00:51:18,150 --> 00:51:19,250
Sun!

666
00:51:19,270 --> 00:51:20,100
Chris!

667
00:51:20,610 --> 00:51:21,880
I'm sorry!

668
00:51:35,990 --> 00:51:45,320
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

669
00:51:45,870 --> 00:51:51,000
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

670
00:51:51,030 --> 00:51:54,640
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

671
00:51:55,370 --> 00:52:01,060
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

672
00:52:01,080 --> 00:52:10,510
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

673
00:52:10,910 --> 00:52:15,960
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

674
00:52:15,980 --> 00:52:20,260
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

675
00:52:20,280 --> 00:52:29,200
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

676
00:52:29,640 --> 00:52:37,800
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
